    {
      "type": "grammar",
      "id": "u24.d01.grammar",
      "title": {
        "en": "Perfect passive: has/have been + V3",
        "ru": "Перфектный пассив: has/have been + V3"
      },
      "rule": {
        "en": "The passive can be used in any tense. In the present perfect passive, use \"has/have been + past participle\" to say something has been done, without saying who did it.",
        "ru": "Пассив можно использовать в любом времени. В present perfect passive — «has/have been + причастие», чтобы сказать, что что-то сделано, не называя, кто."
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "present passive (review)",
            "ru": "настоящий пассив (повтор)"
          },
          "formula": "am/is/are + V3",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "These cars are made in Japan.",
              "ru": "Эти машины делают в Японии."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "passive"
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "present perfect passive",
            "ru": "perfect passive"
          },
          "formula": "has/have been + V3",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "The road has been repaired.",
              "ru": "Дорогу отремонтировали."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "passive-extended"
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "past passive (review)",
            "ru": "прошедший пассив (повтор)"
          },
          "formula": "was/were + V3",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "The bridge was built in 1990.",
              "ru": "Мост построили в 1990."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "passive"
        }
      ],
      "pitfalls": [
        {
          "en": "Perfect passive keeps \"been\": \"has been repaired\", not \"has repaired\" (that's active).",
          "ru": "В перфектном пассиве есть «been»: «has been repaired», а не «has repaired» (это актив)."
        },
        {
          "en": "Use the past participle (V3): \"has been built\", not \"has been build\".",
          "ru": "Нужно причастие (V3): «has been built», а не «has been build»."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "reading",
      "id": "u24.d01.reading",
      "title": {
        "en": "The new bridge",
        "ru": "Новый мост"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "u24.d01.reading.b1",
          "en": "After two years of work, the new bridge has finally been completed. It was designed by a famous engineer and built by a local company. Strong steel and concrete were used to make it safe.",
          "ru": "После двух лет работы новый мост наконец достроен. Его спроектировал известный инженер, а построила местная компания. Для прочности использовали крепкую сталь и бетон.",
          "audio": {
            "src": "media/audio/u24.d01.reading.b1.wav",
            "license": {
              "type": "original",
              "attribution": "Project authors (LLM-assisted)"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "u24.d01.reading.b2",
          "en": "The old bridge, which was built over a hundred years ago, has been closed. \"Everything has been checked and tested,\" said the mayor. \"The new bridge will be opened to traffic next week.\" Thousands of cars are expected every day.",
          "ru": "Старый мост, который построили больше ста лет назад, закрыли. «Всё проверено и испытано, — сказал мэр. — Новый мост откроют для движения на следующей неделе». Ожидаются тысячи машин ежедневно.",
          "audio": {
            "src": "media/audio/u24.d01.reading.b2.wav",
            "license": {
              "type": "original",
              "attribution": "Project authors (LLM-assisted)"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
